    thinking: "**Addressing Build Failures**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag: the build crashed because of ESLint errors. Turns out those checks are baked into the build process, leading to an early exit. I\'m investigating how to handle this better, perhaps configuring the build to ignore `eslint.config.mjs` or to handle it differently.\n\n\n**Resolving ESLint Issues**\n\nI\'m tackling those ESLint errors in `app/page.tsx` now. Fixed the `react/no-unescaped-entities` error by using `&quot;`. The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` is more involved. I am using a `mounted` state variable to avoid synchronous `setState` calls in the effect, mitigating hydration mismatches. The `dateStr` is now only set after component mount.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Updates**\n\nI\'m revisiting the avatar component. Initially, I considered using `next/image` for the dicebear API image but decided against it, simplifying by replacing the dynamic image with a text initial \"A\" for admin. I\'m exploring other options to ensure the avatar displays correctly without introducing complex configurations or dependencies.\n\n\n"
