  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Sidebar**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the sidebar component\'s implementation. I\'m examining the specific CSS classes and conditional logic to understand how the sidebar\'s behavior, especially the width and position, change based on the screen size and the `sidebarOpen` state. I am focusing on the transitions and responsiveness of the sidebar. I\'m hoping to improve its visual appeal and user experience.\n\n\n**Refining the Sidebar Logic**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the sidebar\'s conditional classes, especially concerning width transitions and responsiveness. The `sidebarOpen` state dictates width variations across different screen sizes. I\'ve re-examined the logo area, identifying a discrepancy in the height specification which I will modify to ensure it\'s responsive too. This will hopefully enhance the sidebar\'s overall appearance and ensure a more cohesive user experience.\n\n\n**Updating Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the sidebar\'s navigation elements in `page.tsx`. I\'ve updated the styling of the nav items for a cleaner look. The current `px-3 py-3` is replaced with `px-6 py-3`, and the gap is now `3`. I\'m focusing on improved visual hierarchy by using a border, and reducing text size for clarity. I\'m focusing on the hover and active states using `bg-gradient-to-r` and border changes. I am also updating the active icon using opacity.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Topbar**\n\nI\'m now changing the topbar component. The existing height, background color, border, and padding are being overridden with new specifications using CSS variables to achieve better consistency across the application\'s design. The `h-16` will be replaced with `height: 64px`, `bg-[#0D0D0D]/95` is now `var(--card)`, `border-b` is now `1px solid var(--border)`, and `px-4 lg:px-8` is now `padding: 0 24px`. I am confident that this will align it better visually.\n\n\n**Refining the Search Bar**\n\nI\'m now implementing the search bar, focusing on both the visual appearance and functionality. I\'ve noted that `<div class=\"search-bar\">` had the necessary structure, with the `background` as `var(--bg)`, and `border` being `1px solid var(--border)`. I have set the `border-radius` to 6px, and padding to `8px 12px`, with the width to `300px`, and the text as 13px. I\'ll integrate the search functionality in the topbar.\n\n\n**Implementing the Topbar**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user actions within the topbar. I have incorporated a notifications icon with a visual indicator, the date display, and user profile information in the topbar. The styling is now updated to follow existing conventions, and to use the same variables. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual consistency of this section with the rest of the application. The notifications are using the bell icon, and the user display is the rounded initials display, with the user role below.\n\n\n**Revising the StatCard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \'StatCard\' component within the dashboard view. I\'ve noted that while the existing `StatCard` component\'s props are different, I can update the styling. I\'ll need to maintain current functionality while aligning the visual presentation with the new specifications. Specifically, I\'ll focus on visual consistency, without making changes to functionality.\n\n\n**Updating the StatCard**\n\nI\'m now changing the `StatCard` component. Rather than mocking data, I\'m refactoring the existing component based on the provided HTML structure. I\'ll maintain the current props, but adjust the styling to align with the design: 12px uppercase for labels, 24px bold font for values, and a 10px text display. I\'ll preserve existing functionality.\n\n\n**Adapting the StatCard**\n\nI\'m now integrating the styling for the `StatCard` component. While the existing React code includes icons, and HTML doesn\'t, I\'ll be sure to preserve the icons as instructed, as long as it does not restructure HTML elements. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency, and adapting the existing code to use the right styling. I\'ll maintain functionality and the layout.\n\n\n**Refining the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now implementing the section header for the dashboard view. I\'m adding a heading with the main title and a subtitle, adjusting the styling to match the design\'s font and size. The header is placed at the top of the component. I am using the `mb-6` margin to add spacing between the header and other elements.\n\n\n**Updating Panel Structures**\n\nI\'m now changing the panel components, starting with visual changes. The wrapper `div` gets a flex container with a fixed height. The header is adjusted with the right padding and border. I\'ve re-styled the `h3` title, updating the font and size. The select element now has a new look, with updated colors, font and padding. The right panel is updated, and I\'ve ensured a consistent styling.\n\n\n**Styling the Activity**\n\nI\'m now styling the activity rows within the panel component, focusing on the visual display of user check-in data. I\'m formatting the user\'s name, timestamp, and plan details for clarity. I\'ve ensured a consistent `text-[13px]` font size and border treatments to maintain visual hierarchy. I\'m focusing on responsiveness.\n\n\n"
