  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Members Section**\n\nI\'m currently focused on building out the \"Members\" section within the Corenix Club Software app. I\'ve been detailing the requirements: ensuring it shows when `activeTab` is \'Members\', the top bar with a search box (name/phone), a filter dropdown (All/Active/Expired/Paused), and a red \"+ Add Member\" button. Finally, the Member Table structure is top of mind.\n\n\n**Defining Member Display Fields**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member data display, finalizing the table columns: Avatar (initials), Name, Phone, Membership Type, Start/Expiry Dates, Amount Paid, and Status badge. Actions will be View, Edit, Delete, and a WhatsApp icon. I\'m also preparing sample data and considering sort options by name and expiry.\nI\'m also working on sorting and filtering, as well as the \'add member\' modal and member profile page.\n\n\n**Finalizing Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now detailing the application\'s state management, specifically focusing on handling filter, sort, and modal states. I\'ve defined `sortConfig`, `isAddModalOpen`, and `selectedMember` for seamless user interactions. I am now working on how data is displayed given different user requests.\n\n\n**Integrating the New Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `MembersView`, `MemberProfile`, and `AddMemberModal` components into `app/page.tsx`. I\'ll also add Lucide icons for actions such as `Edit` and `Trash`. I plan to integrate the existing code I have created to display the new data.\n\n\n**Refactoring and Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now changing my focus, moving from component integration towards structuring the `MembersView` component in pure JavaScript, HTML, and CSS, as the project requires. This involves setting up the state variables for search, filter, sort, add modal, and selected member, within the new context. I\'m focusing on incorporating relevant Lucide icons. I\'ve switched gears and am now ready to begin the work.\n\n\n**Adapting Frameworks for New Code**\n\nI\'ve realized the project\'s codebase is Next.js + Tailwind, and I\'ll keep the existing framework as directed, rather than the pure JS approach I was pursuing. I\'m focusing on updating `app/page.tsx` to handle the different views. I am preparing to implement the `MembersView`, `MemberProfile`, and `AddMemberModal`. I\'m also preparing the required Lucide icons for the functionality.\n\n\n**Building the UI Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `MembersView` component, handling search, filter, and sort states. I\'ve also added `AddMemberModal`, including its state and visibility toggle, along with the `MemberProfile` component. I\'ve ensured a high z-index for the modal using `fixed inset-0 z-50`. Finally, I\'m working on the data structure for the mocked member data.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating filtering and sorting functionality. I\'ve implemented logic to filter members based on search terms (name and phone) and status. Further, I\'ve incorporated sorting by name and expiry date, with ascending and descending options. Finally, I\'ve applied the filter and sort results to display the data.\n\n\n**Refining Search and Filters**\n\nI\'m now refining the search and filter features, focusing on user interaction and data responsiveness. The search input is implemented with search icon, placeholder text, and state management. The filter dropdown with different options has been implemented. I\'m focusing on the implementation with the select input and option components. I\'m now testing the code.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the members table header and action buttons within the UI components. I\'ve built the filter and add buttons in the header, including the functionality to open the \"Add Member\" modal, as well as the column sorting by name and date, using sorting states. I\'m focusing on the click handlers.\n\n\n**Finalizing Sortable Member Columns**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the members table header and sortable columns. I\'ve integrated sort direction indicators with name and expiry columns. I\'m focusing on the click handlers for these columns and ensuring they trigger the correct sorting logic for a seamless UI update.\n\n\n**Implementing the Table Rows**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member table rows, mapping the `filteredMembers` data to display the content. I\'m focusing on incorporating the `AddMemberModal` component within the current structure. I\'m reviewing the current code\'s impact on UI and data updates.\n\n\n**Adding Member Profile Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating new components, and I\'m currently working on the structure of the `AddMemberModal` component within the current structure. I\'m focusing on the implementation of table rows and integrating other parts of the table. I will review the code to ensure UI and data updates.\n\n\n**Adding Member Field Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the input fields for adding members, focusing on `FullName` and `PhoneNumber`. I\'m using appropriate HTML input types and styling for a consistent user experience. I\'m also adding placeholders and label elements for accessibility and clarity. I will continue to add fields.\n\n\n**Adding Member Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member addition form with email and date of birth fields. I\'ve designed the layout as a grid, including labels, placeholders, and proper styling. The input types and attributes are set for an improved user experience. The color scheme is now set to dark. I\'m focusing on user interface consistency.\n\n\n**Adding Membership Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the select input for gender. I\'ve also integrated the select input for the membership plan. I\'ve finalized the implementation, and I\'m currently working on incorporating this into the application. I will focus on the front end.\n\n\n**Adding Membership Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the membership and start date inputs within the \"Add Member\" form. Specifically, I\'m working on the membership plan select input with monthly to annual options and a date picker. I\'m focusing on their implementation and styling for a seamless user experience. I will now integrate the data.\n\n\n**Integrating Payment Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the payment details into the \"Add Member\" form. I\'m focusing on the \"Payment Mode\" select input with options for Cash, UPI, and Card. Also, I\'m working on the \"Amount Paid\" input field with the rupee symbol. I\'m focusing on their implementation and styling for a user-friendly experience.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the modal content with input components, finalizing form submission handling and improving the overall user experience. I\'ve been focusing on integrating date and payment details, and I will focus on user interface consistency. I\'m now testing the code.\n\n\n**Enhancing Profile Display**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member profile card, focusing on a responsive, concise display. I\'m prioritizing the layout with flexbox, ensuring the avatar, name, phone, and join date are clearly presented. I\'m also preparing to use the Contact and Calendar icons.\n\n\n**Styling Status Badges**\n\nI\'m now implementing the member status badges, including \"Active\", \"Expired\", and \"Paused\". I\'m using dynamic classes for color-coding, and implementing the membership plan badge to align with the design specifications. I\'m ensuring they display correctly within the table rows, along with the edit profile button. I\'ve switched to implementing a new structure to display the data.\n\n\n**Refining Page Layout**\n\nI\'m now detailing the member profile layout within `page.tsx`, specifically the visual organization. I\'m focusing on incorporating payment history, visit history, and key details within a responsive grid structure for clearer presentation. I\'m also planning the placement of \"Receipt\" and \"Renew\" buttons for easy access. The integration will need careful data management.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 46
      nanos: 961773849
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
