  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Attendance Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on the \"Attendance\" section, and I\'ve started breaking down the components. The first focus will be the \"QUICK CHECK-IN\" panel, and I\'m detailing the key elements: a large search box, a matching member card, and a prominent \"Mark Attendance\" button. I\'ll need to define the success and expiration message outputs. The second portion will be the \"FINGERPRINT SECTION\".\n\n\n**Adding Attendance Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the fingerprint card, with a device integration status indicator. Today\'s attendance log will be implemented as a table, showing total visitors and an export CSV function. Also, I\'m working on the attendance history tab, including date pickers and a monthly calendar heatmap. I\'m updating the icons import in `page.tsx` now, including `Fingerprint`, `Calendar` and other needed components. Finally, I\'m integrating the `<AttendanceView />`.\n\n\n**Defining Attendance Component**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `AttendanceView` component. I\'m focusing on the state variables, including `searchQuery`, `selectedMember`, `checkInStatus`, and `activeTab`. I\'m using mock data for members and check-ins, which will be integrated for the initial state. I\'m also now structuring the component with the tab selection (`today` vs `history`), and setting up the basic search functionality with a minimal length requirement. I\'m planning out the state updates based on the user\'s search query input.\n\n\n**Implementing Search & State**\n\nI\'m now refining the search and check-in logic within the AttendanceView. I\'m focusing on the implementation of `handleSearch`, making sure it\'s accurate and efficient, including the member matching logic. The `handleCheckIn` function sets the `checkInStatus` to \'success\'. I\'m also ensuring the state updates seamlessly.\n\n\n**Structuring Attendance Layout**\n\nI\'m now integrating the structure of the `AttendanceView` component. My focus is on the tabbed layout, including \"Today\" and \"History & Heatmap\". The \"Today\" tab has a grid layout, splitting into \"Quick Check-in\" and \"Today\'s Log Table\". The \"History\" tab will display the calendar heatmap. I am currently working on the layout within the active tab conditions.\n\n\n**Designing Quick Check-in UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Quick Check-in UI components. I\'ve designed the heading and search input, including placeholder text, and implemented the search icon, as well as the input styling. I\'m now integrating the member card display. I\'m making sure all the input features and the component structure is accurate, as well as considering accessibility, and responsive design, to create an intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Refining Member Check-in**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the member information within the Quick Check-in UI. I\'m dynamically rendering the member\'s name, phone, and plan, and integrating the member\'s status (expired or active) with conditional UI elements. I\'m displaying expiry information if the member\'s membership has lapsed, and enabling a \"Mark Attendance\" button otherwise. I\'ve also implemented success messaging for check-in completions.\n\n\n**Integrating Check-in Messaging**\n\nI\'ve integrated a success message within the check-in UI, including a checkmark icon, the member\'s name, and a motivational message. I\'m focusing on making the message prominent and visually appealing to provide positive feedback. I\'m now integrating the biometric system UI elements.\n\n\n**Adding Biometric Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the biometric device connection button, and defining the device status indicator, which will be a central part of the fingerprint section. I\'m focusing on the UI integration of a connect button, to link the biometric system with the attendance tracking. I am currently working on the table, to display a log of current visitors.\n\n\n**Implementing Attendance Log**\n\nI\'m now implementing the attendance log table. I\'m focusing on rendering data, including serial numbers, member names, phone numbers, check-in times, and membership types. I\'ve designed the table with a clear, concise layout, including column headers and row data. I\'m also adding a status column with conditional styling.\n\n\n**Developing History Feature**\n\nI\'m now implementing the attendance history section. I\'ve integrated a date picker for selecting specific dates, and I\'m adding the monthly footfall heatmap display. I\'m focusing on making the selection and display intuitive. The date picker and heatmap UI will integrate within the History tab, offering easy access to historical attendance data. I am currently working on the UI of both components.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 25
      nanos: 847536106
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
