  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Missing Icons**\n\nI\'ve made progress on incorporating the missing icons. I\'ve successfully added `Briefcase`, `Clock`, `Phone`, `ShieldCheck`, `Award`, `Activity`, `Coffee`, `User`, and `Wallet` to the `lucide-react` imports. Next, I\'m integrating these new components into the active tab render list within the code.\n\n\n**Defining New Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the components needed for the `StaffView` and `TrainersView`. For `StaffView`, I\'ll implement staff cards with key details, an \"add staff\" modal, a staff attendance table, and a monthly summary. The `TrainersView` components will include trainer profiles with specific attributes, a full profile view, an \"add trainer\" modal, and a trainer performance section. My next step will be coding the basic structure for these views.\n\n\n**Refining Implementations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the implementations for `StaffView` and `TrainersView`. I\'m concerned about potential token limits, so I\'m aiming for concise yet robust code. To ensure feasibility, I\'m currently prototyping the code directly in text, creating mock data like the `MOCK_STAFF` variable as an example. This process will help to streamline the structure and implementation.\n\n\n**Developing Staff Cards**\n\nI\'ve started building the structure for the `StaffView` cards. I\'m focusing on displaying key information, including avatar, salary, and join date. The code for the header, \"Staff Management\", is in place. I have included an \"Add Staff\" button. Currently, I\'m working on populating the grid with mock data.\n\n\n**Implementing Staff Status**\n\nI\'m now integrating staff status indicators into the staff cards. I\'m focusing on visual cues; for example, the top bar changes color based on presence. Additionally, I\'m adding `Phone` icons next to phone numbers to enhance readability within each staff card, as well as an associated phone number. I\'m also ensuring the overall design is clear and concise.\n\n\n**Refining Display Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the display elements within staff cards. I\'ve added a shift display, including a clock icon for clarity, and am formatting the information to be easily readable. I\'m also including status indicators, using color to convey information about each staff member. The attendance table is under construction, and I\'m ensuring it\'s clearly organized.\n\n\n**Constructing Attendance Table**\n\nI\'m now building the attendance table for the staff cards and focused on the table\'s structure. I\'m using mock staff data to populate the table. My goal is to clearly display staff names, roles, in times, and current status, all within a small, easily scannable format. I\'m focusing on text styling and colors to keep the information clear.\n\n\n**Finalizing Table Implementation**\n\nI\'ve completed the attendance table; it displays staff names, roles, in-times, and status concisely. The final touch was refining the monthly summary display. I\'ve ensured all elements are clearly presented and formatted. The entire table is optimized for readability.\n\n\n**Evaluating Staff Progress**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating the staff progress display and integrated percentage-based progress bars within each staff card, showing attendance. The visual status cues enhance readability. I\'ve also added the `AddStaffModal` to maintain overall clarity. I\'m satisfied with the current progress.\n\n\n**Designing Add Staff Modal**\n\nI\'m now designing the \"Add New Staff\" modal. I\'ve structured it with a clear header, a close button using an `X` icon, and a form with a grid layout for input fields. The modal uses a dark theme with a backdrop blur. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness and visual clarity in the layout.\n\n\n**Structuring Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now structuring the input fields within the \"Add New Staff\" modal. I\'ve added name, phone, and role fields. I\'m focusing on ensuring these fields are well-labeled and easy to use, utilizing a dark theme to match the existing design. I\'m paying close attention to visual consistency and user-friendly formatting.\n\n\n**Adding Shift Time Input**\n\nI\'m now incorporating shift time input fields into the \"Add New Staff\" modal. I\'ve designed the fields for start and end times, using a dark theme with the appropriate labels. My goal is to streamline the input process with well-labeled and easy-to-use time selection for the user. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency.\n\n\n**Adding Salary Input**\n\nI\'m now integrating the salary input fields in the \"Add New Staff\" modal. I\'ve included a currency symbol for visual clarity and am focusing on formatting the input to be user-friendly. I\'m also adding a \"Join Date\" field for complete staff information. I\'m making sure it matches the existing dark theme for consistency.\n\n\n\n**Developing Trainer Views**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `TrainersView` component and have mocked some data to populate a display. I am creating trainer profiles with associated attributes, along with a full profile view. I am also planning an \"add trainer\" modal, similar to the \"Add Staff\" modal. I am thinking about how to integrate a section to showcase trainer performance.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Trainer Display**\n\nI\'m now building out the trainer display, including trainer cards with key details. The aim is to create a clear and informative layout. I\'m focusing on attributes like trainer names, specializations, and availability within the trainer cards, so it\'s a useful presentation of each trainer.\n\n\n**Analyzing Trainer Performance**\n\nI\'m now incorporating performance metrics within the `TrainersView`. I\'m focusing on key indicators, like sessions held and fees collected, to provide an overview. These metrics will be displayed within visually distinct, informative sections. I\'m prioritizing clear presentation of the performance data.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating Trainer Data**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the trainer data and display structure. I\'m focusing on incorporating trainer status indicators into the trainer cards, for clear visual distinction. I\'m adding `Status` indicators to each card. I\'m also ensuring the overall trainer data presentation is concise, as well as easy to read.\n\n\n**Refining Trainer Status**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual presentation of trainer statuses. I\'ve added a status indicator, a status display (e.g., Active), and incorporated the display in each trainer card for clear distinctions. Additionally, I\'m ensuring the data is presented clearly and concisely.\n\n\n**Integrating Trainer Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the modal for adding new trainers. I have also been focused on the layout of trainer cards. I\'ve included phone icons and made sure that each card is visually distinct. I\'m also preparing the trainer cards, including phone numbers, and including a \"view profile\" element. I\'ve finished the initial structure and now I\'m working on the design.\n\n\n**Adding Trainer Data**\n\nI\'ve integrated the form for adding trainers, including fields for full name and phone number. I\'m focusing on ensuring these inputs are user-friendly within the dark theme. Next, I plan to add additional details to complete the trainer profile, focusing on overall user experience.\n\n\n\n**Adding Specialization Input**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specialization and experience input fields within the \"Add New Trainer\" modal. I\'m using a select dropdown for specializations and a number input for experience. The goal is to provide intuitive, user-friendly forms with appropriate formatting. I am aiming to ensure visual consistency with the existing design.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Salary Input**\n\nI\'ve completed integrating the salary input, now with a placeholder to illustrate the format. I\'ve finished the input fields for join date. All relevant information is now included, and the modal is functioning as expected. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness and final adjustments.\n\n\n**Finalizing Trainer Bio**\n\nI\'m now integrating the trainer bio/notes section into the trainer form, including a `textarea` field for detailed information. I\'ve also incorporated cancel and save buttons within the form\'s footer. My focus is on ensuring comprehensive and user-friendly trainer profiles within the new modal.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing Trainer Progress**\n\nI\'m now implementing the back button and trainer data. I\'ve integrated a back button with an arrow icon. I\'ve also incorporated the trainer\'s name and avatar into the display. I\'m focusing on ensuring data is correctly populated and presented. I am also working on adding the name, avatar, and trainer status with visual indicators.\n\n\n**Refining Trainer Profile**\n\nI\'m now refining the structure of the `TrainersView` cards and integrating details. I\'ve successfully added status displays and included specialization and experience indicators. I\'m focusing on making the cards visually appealing, and integrating the trainer\'s bio and an edit profile button. I\'m also including a message button to improve the overall design.\n\n\n**Constructing Schedule Displays**\n\nI\'m now building out the schedule display components. I\'m focusing on a clear presentation for timing and scheduling. I\'ve got the basic structure for the schedule display including a header with a clock icon. I have also added a visual timetable, as well as an associated display for the next session. Next, I\'ll integrate the new components.\n\n\n**Integrating Member Displays**\n\nI\'m now integrating the member displays into the trainer cards. I\'m focusing on a clean presentation of assigned members, using mock data for now. I\'m adding a counter for the number of members, creating a grid layout for individual member displays with avatars and names. Next, I\'ll link the mock member data.\n\n\n**Integrating Member Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the MemberDisplay components. I\'ve successfully added `Member`, `List`, `User2`, and `Eye` from `lucide-react`. I\'m updating the active tab render list to include a new section for member displays, focusing on a clean and intuitive presentation of each member\'s information within the trainer cards.\n\n\n\n"
