*Integrating Chart Displays**\n\nI\'m now integrating the bar chart data for revenue visualization and configuring its display options for responsiveness and the removal of the legend. I have also added pie chart data for different report frequency types with tailored colors and a bottom-aligned legend.\n\n\n**Adding Summary Cards**\n\nI\'m now integrating summary cards to present key revenue metrics, employing a grid layout for responsive display. Each card showcases total, cash, and online revenue figures with styled text and appropriate colours and currency.\n\n\n**Adding Member Summary Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating new member summary data into the existing dashboard. I\'ve built new cards that will display key figures. Each card will show new members, renewals, and active members, all styled with a consistent design, leveraging the grid layout for responsiveness. I\'m focusing on text styling and colors.\n\n\n**Visualizing Revenue Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating revenue data visualizations. I\'m focusing on a bar chart for revenue breakdown and a pie chart to display membership types, enhancing visual clarity with data and responsive designs. My aim is to create engaging and informative displays.\n\n\n**Constructing Transaction Tables**\n\nI\'m now integrating transaction tables for detailed reporting. I\'m focusing on a responsive, data-rich table layout with date, member name, amount, type, mode, and receipt number columns. I\'m prioritizing styling for legibility.\n\n\n**Building Transaction Tables**\n\nI\'m now focusing on transaction table design and incorporating transaction data. I\'m prioritizing data display and adding styling with a responsive table. I\'ve designed columns with dates, member names, and transaction details, and I am focused on the layout. I am also working on adding a conditional display to make the tables data-rich.\n\n\n**Enhancing Summary Cards**\n\nI\'m now integrating new summary cards, focusing on key metrics like collection today