  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Code Edits**\n\nI\'m starting by preparing multiple edits to `/app/page.tsx` using `default_api:multi_edit_file`. I\'ve outlined new component code logic, focusing on an `OffersView` function with state for a modal\'s open/close state. The plan is to enhance the existing structure with improved state handling.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating a button to open a \"Create New Offer\" modal within the `/app/page.tsx` file, along with a header. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, utilizing Tailwind classes for layout, including a `Plus` icon for the button. The goal is a clean, user-friendly interface for adding promotions.\n\n\n**Adding Offer Cards**\n\nI\'m presently building upon the UI, integrating promotional offer cards within `/app/page.tsx`. I\'m designing these with distinct layouts and Tailwind classes. Each card has a title, description, and an icon, aiming for a consistent visual language. My focus is on visual clarity and user interaction.\n\n\n**Constructing Offer Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating a new component that presents information about \"Referral Bonus\" offers, incorporating a visual layout with text and an icon for clarity. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual balance. The goal is to provide a clean and intuitive display of promotional details.\n\n\n**Developing Table Structures**\n\nI\'m presently focused on a table component within `/app/page.tsx` designed to display promotional campaign data. I\'ve defined column headers for campaign name, target audience, send date, response count, and status. I\'m implementing dynamic rows with example data and hover effects for improved usability. My objective is to deliver a concise, easily readable table layout for promotional campaign overviews.\n\n\n**Finalizing Campaign Table**\n\nI\'m finalizing the promotional campaign table. I\'m focusing on responsiveness by adding more CSS styling, including hover effects, and making sure the text and date format are correct. The final touches are on the conditional formatting for status display. I am now creating an offer modal and integrating it within the main page to ensure a seamless workflow for users.\n\n\n**Designing Offer Modal**\n\nI\'m now focused on the offer modal\'s visual elements within `/app/page.tsx`. I\'m creating the header with a title, \"Create & Send Offer,\" and a close button, ensuring its responsiveness with Tailwind classes. I am also working on the modal\'s internal structure and how the information will be presented. The layout is set up with a two-column grid using Tailwind, preparing it for input fields.\n\n\n**Implementing Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now integrating input fields within the offer modal in `/app/page.tsx`. I\'m working on the design for fields labeled \"Offer Name,\" \"Discount Percentage,\" \"Valid Till,\" and \"Target Audience,\" each styled with Tailwind and placeholder text to enhance user experience. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual consistency.\n\n\n**Refining Form Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the form elements within the offer modal in `/app/page.tsx`. I\'ve added a select dropdown component for \'Target Audience\', and I am working on a textarea for \'Add Message Text\', both styled for visual consistency and user experience. The design choices prioritize clarity.\n\n\n\n**Previewing WhatsApp Display**\n\nI\'m now previewing a WhatsApp message within the offer modal in `/app/page.tsx`. I\'ve constructed a visual preview section with a smartphone icon, and a background image. The mock-up includes placeholder text with dynamic elements. I am adding final visual refinements for user clarity.\n\n\n**Integrating Sending Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the logic to send offers via WhatsApp. I\'m focusing on the integration of a send method radio button within the `/app/page.tsx` file to allow users to select between different sending methods. I\'m prioritizing user experience and ensuring a seamless workflow.\n\n\n**Adding Send Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating an SMS sending option within the `/app/page.tsx` file to complement the WhatsApp functionality. I\'ve designed a visually distinct button with a message icon, using styling to highlight its function. I\'m focusing on providing users with a clear choice for sending methods.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Member Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating a member display section. I\'m focusing on incorporating a member\'s name and creating a line graph using chartjs to visualize weight measurements over time. The graph is being designed to be responsive, with custom styling for enhanced readability and visual appeal. I\'m prioritizing data clarity and user engagement.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Member Select**\n\nI\'m now integrating a member selection component using a dropdown within the `/app/page.tsx` file. I\'ve styled this with a custom border and a search icon. I\'ve designed the select element to display the names of existing members for user convenience, focusing on a visually clean and intuitive interface. I\'m prioritizing ease of access to member data.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Member Engagement**\n\nI\'m now analyzing member engagement. I\'ve designed a section to highlight that fifteen members have not updated their body measurements this month. I\'ve included a button that will send them a reminder. I\'m focusing on user action and data tracking.\n\n\n**Adding Measurement Inputs**\n\nI\'m now integrating new input fields within `/app/page.tsx` for member measurements: \'Weight (kg)\' and \'Height (cm)\'. I\'ve styled them with Tailwind, and implemented placeholder text to guide the user. I\'m focusing on visual consistency and data entry accuracy.\n\n\n**Adding Body Measurements**\n\nI\'m now integrating additional member measurement inputs within `/app/page.tsx` for \"Chest (in)\" and \"Waist (in).\" I\'m working with Tailwind to style these, aiming for visual consistency alongside the \"Body Fat (%)\" field. I want to provide a comprehensive and intuitive input experience for users.\n\n\n**Incorporating Measurement Fields**\n\nI\'m now integrating new fields within the member area of `/app/page.tsx`, specifically for \"Arms (in)\". I\'m styling these inputs using Tailwind to match the design. I also included a \"Save Measurement\" button with visual feedback on click. My focus remains on data entry efficiency and a consistent UI.\n\n\n**Visualizing Data Trends**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"Progress Chart: Weight\" section within `/app/page.tsx`, and I\'m adding a button to send reports via WhatsApp. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual balance. I\'m also including a line chart using `Chart.js` to clearly display weight measurements over time. My focus is on providing actionable insights through a user-friendly interface.\n\n\n**Displaying Measurement History**\n\nI\'m now integrating a measurement history table within the `/app/page.tsx` file, specifically for displaying a member\'s data. I\'ve designed the table with headers for date, weight, BMI, body fat, chest, waist, and arms. I\'m focusing on ensuring clarity, visual consistency, and a responsive layout for easy data review. I\'m also including date formatting and units of measurement.\n\n\n**Adding Review Sections**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \'ReviewsView\' component within `/app/page.tsx`, and I\'ve focused on creating a clear visual structure. I\'m building it with a card design, aiming to effectively display user feedback and ratings. The design emphasizes user experience, with concise and easily digestible information.\n\n\n**Filtering Review Sections**\n\nI\'m now integrating filter buttons within the \'ReviewsView\' component in `/app/page.tsx`, designed to refine the display by star rating. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, styling with Tailwind, and ensuring the UI remains clear and user-friendly. The functionality is designed to refine user feedback and ratings.\n\n\n\n**Refining Review Card Layout**\n\nI\'m now building upon the \'ReviewsView\' in `/app/page.tsx` with a refined review card layout. I\'ve focused on visual clarity, including a star rating display and user feedback details. The design emphasizes user experience, with a concise and easily digestible information. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual balance.\n\n\n**Constructing Review Inputs**\n\nI\'m now integrating rating selection and text input components within the `ReviewsView` section of `/app/page.tsx`. I\'ve constructed a styled dropdown for rating and a textarea for detailed reviews, with border, padding, and text styling. My goal is to add intuitive methods for user feedback, enhancing data collection.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Review Cards**\n\nI\'m now integrating individual review cards within the `ReviewsView` component of `/app/page.tsx`. I\'m focusing on incorporating user names, ratings, comments, and the date. My design prioritizes clear presentation of feedback, using consistent styling with Tailwind for responsiveness and visual appeal.\n\n\n**Integrating Review Actions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding interactive elements within each review card in `/app/page.tsx`. I\'m working on including a copy button to enable sharing of user feedback and reviews. Also, I\'m integrating logic to display the initials from the user name inside the circular avatar. The goal is enhanced user interaction.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m now displaying the user\'s initials, and the review date, for each review item to ensure readability. I also am making the rating be properly displayed using a loop of stars. Next, I\'m integrating the button component with hover effects, to indicate when the review can be copied to the clipboard.\n\n\n"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_MAX_TOKENS
  }
}
