    thinking: "**Developing Notification System**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"Corenix\" app\'s notification system. I\'ve designed a bell icon with a dynamic pending count for the top bar. The dropdown will show members expiring today (red), birthdays today (blue), members with 0 visits this week, and staff absent today. The visual design is prioritized to convey the critical information in a concise manner.\n\n\n**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'ve been working on new features for \"Corenix\". I\'m implementing a global search bar in the top bar with categorized dropdown results. I\'m also building a settings section with gym details, pricing editors, WhatsApp settings, and admin password change. Finally, I\'m designing a receipt generator to provide printable receipts with all necessary details and a print button. I will also be polishing the UI for a smoother user experience, including page transitions, loading spinners, confirmation dialogs, and mobile-friendly tables. I will then work on a light/dark mode toggle.\n\n\n**Considering Dark/Light Mode**\n\nI\'m now contemplating the dark/light mode toggle implementation. Given the hardcoded color values and the constraint of this project, a full theme switch seems complex right now. I\'ll implement a toggle button, possibly displaying a toast message saying \"Theme switching coming soon\" to manage expectations. I might add a class to the wrapper and override colors via JS or CSS. I\'ll also add Corenix branding in the header.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Design**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual design. I envision a subtle red glow gradient for the dashboard to enhance its aesthetics. I\'m also breaking down the changes to the settings section: adding \'Settings\' to navItems. The global search implementation involves a search query state and a dropdown display. I\'ll add states for the notifications bell icon and receipt generation modals.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
