  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have initialized Firebase in your project! \n\nThe automatic Firebase setup tool encountered an authentication limit from Google Cloud when creating the project database on your behalf. However, since the Corenix Club Software we are building here is actually a modern **React (Next.js) application** rather than a plain vanilla HTML file, I have followed the best practices for this framework.\n\nI installed the `firebase` npm package and created a dedicated `firebase.ts` utility file for initialization and documentation.\n\nHere is the setup that has been added to your applet under `/lib/firebase.ts`. It includes the full collection structure documentation you requested:\n\n```typescript\nimport { initializeApp, getApps, getApp } from \"firebase/app\";\nimport { getAuth } from \"firebase/auth\";\nimport { getFirestore } from \"firebase/firestore\";\nimport { getStorage } from \"firebase/storage\";\nimport { getFunctions } from \"firebase/functions\";\n\n// Replace these placeholder values with your actual Firebase project configuration\nconst firebaseConfig = {\n  apiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY || \"YOUR_API_KEY\",\n  authDomain: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN || \"YOUR_AUTH_DOMAIN\",\n  projectId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID || \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID\",\n  storageBucket: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET || \"YOUR_STORAGE_BUCKET\",\n  messagingSenderId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID || \"YOUR_SENDER_ID\",\n  appId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID || \"YOUR_APP_ID\"\n};\n\n// Initialize Firebase\nconst app = !getApps().length ? initializeApp(firebaseConfig) : getApp();\n\n// Initialize Firebase Services\nconst auth = getAuth(app);\nconst db = getFirestore(app);\nconst storage = getStorage(app);\nconst functions = getFunctions(app);\n\nexport { app, auth, db, storage, functions };\n\n/*\n=========================================================\nFIRESTORE COLLECTIONS STRUCTURE\n=========================================================\n\nCollection: members\nDocument fields: memberId(auto), name, phone, email, dob, gender,\nmembershipPlan, startDate, expiryDate, amountPaid, paymentMode,\ntrainerAssigned, photoURL, fingerprintId, status(active/expired/paused),\ncreatedAt, updatedAt\n\nCollection: attendance\nDocument fields: attendanceId(auto), memberId, memberName, memberPhone,\ncheckInTime, checkInDate, membershipType, memberStatus\n\nCollection: payments\nDocument fields: paymentId(auto), memberId, memberName, amount, \npaymentMode(cash/upi/card), paymentType(new/renewal), planName,\nreceiptNumber, date, createdBy, notes\n\nCollection: staff\nDocument fields: staffId(auto), name, phone, role, shiftStart, \nshiftEnd, salary, joinDate, status, photoURL\n\nCollection: trainers\nDocument fields: trainerId(auto), name, phone, specialization,\nexperience, salary, timing, bio, assignedMembers[], photoURL, status\n\nCollection: measurements\nDocument fields: measurementId(auto), memberId, memberName, date,\nweight, height, bodyFat, chest, waist, arms, bmi(auto-calculated)\n\nCollection: offers\nDocument fields: offerId(auto), title, description, discount,\nvalidTill, targetType, targetPlan, sentAt, sentCount, createdBy\n\nCollection: reviews\nDocument fields: reviewId(auto), memberId, memberName, rating,\nreviewText, date, reply\n\nCollection: settings\nSingle document: gymName, address, phone, whatsappNumber, \nworkingHours, logoURL, membershipPlans[]\n\nCollection: expenses (for future phase)\nCollection: leads (for future phase)\n\n=========================================================\n*/\n```\n\nI have also updated your `.env.example` file so you can go over to your AI Studio Secrets panel whenever you are ready and add real credentials like `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=\"\"`.\n\nLet me know once you have configured your actual Firebase config, or if you\'d like me to start migrating specific frontend operations (like \"Add Member\", \"Check-in\", or \"Settings\") over to read/write directly to this Firebase connection!"
