  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Firebase Security**\n\nI\'m working on the Firebase integration, specifically focusing on the authentication and database interactions. I\'ve begun to translate the provided Firebase logic, concentrating on establishing secure access control and data management using `signInWithEmailAndPassword`, `onAuthStateChanged`, and `signOut` for user authentication, and `doc`, `getDoc`, `collection`, `getDocs`, and `deleteDoc` for document operations in firestore. I\'m keen on establishing robust security measures as the priority here.\n\n\n**Refining Application Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the login state management from `app/page.tsx` into the updated `CorenixApp` structure. I\'m focusing on user state, role assignment, and authentication status. I\'m also addressing UI state variables such as loading, login errors, and the sidebar\'s open state.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the `onAuthStateChanged` function. I\'m focusing on user data retrieval from Firestore based on the authenticated user ID. I\'m analyzing the logic for setting the user role and tab selection based on retrieved data or fallback values, particularly for cases where user data doesn\'t exist in Firestore. The error handling, especially the fallback to \'admin\' role in case of errors, is of particular interest.\n\n\n**Evaluating Login UI and Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on the login functionality. I am examining the `handleLogin` function\'s error handling and user feedback mechanisms. I\'m prioritizing user experience with loading states and error messages. I\'m also ensuring the authentication flow integrates well with the overall app\'s state management, especially the `user` state. I\'m also checking the logic used to handle `null` user data from firebase to ensure a clean slate on log out.\n\n\n**Reviewing Login Form Implementation**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the integration of the login form within the overall UI. I\'m focusing on the visual styling, responsiveness, and accessibility of the form components. I\'m carefully reviewing the use of Tailwind classes for visual elements, ensuring the form aligns with the application\'s design language and maintains a clean user experience. I\'m also confirming the form\'s responsiveness across various screen sizes.\n\n\n**Assessing Login Form Styling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the finer details of the login form\'s styling. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy, reviewing the use of Tailwind classes, and ensuring consistent design language. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the spacing, font sizes, and color contrasts to ensure visual appeal and accessibility. I\'m checking the form field\'s responsiveness across different devices to guarantee a consistent user experience. I\'m also ensuring the error message displays effectively and is visually distinct.\n\n\n**Validating Role-Based Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the role-based navigation logic within the application. I\'m verifying the `allowedNavItems` array is correctly filtering menu items according to user roles, specifically for \'admin\', \'receptionist\', and \'trainer\' roles. I\'m checking the logic to ensure that based on the `role` variable, the navigation options are restricted appropriately. I\'m also reviewing how the `role` is derived earlier in the code.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 26
      nanos: 417249631
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
